mental-poker (https://github.com/paritytech/mental-poker)

Upstream declares `license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"` in every crate's Cargo.toml
and in its README, but does not ship the license files. We use it under the
MIT license, whose text follows.

The README's wording has changed: until upstream commit 7026b2b (2026-02-08,
"Still MIT OR Apache-2.0") it said work from 2025 on was AGPL-3.0-or-later;
since then it says "Through 2025, this crate is licensed under either of"
MIT or Apache-2.0. The commit we pin (ac4fb67, 2026-09-02) is past 2025, so
that wording doesn't plainly cover it; Cargo.toml still says MIT OR Apache-2.0.

